  "worked_solution": "Solving our equation for $z,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{2z}{3}=4{x}^{2}-6{y}^{2}\\,\u27f9\\,z=6{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\u27e8x,y,z\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8x,\\,y,\\,6{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$   \n\nTherefore, the third component of $f$ is $6{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}.$",
